gmif-check.sh writes (assert (! c :named c)) -- the assertion name and the
declared constant share a symbol. Z3 rejects every such file:
  (error "line 1 column 11: invalid named expression, declaration already
          defined with this name c")
The script redirects stderr into the result file, greps for sat or unsat,
finds neither, and falls through to SAT.
Observed: reported SAT on an island that asserted a claim and its negation.
